# heightfield_project

- Label: HeightField Project
- Category: Copernicus (`Cop`), Houdini 22.0.368
- Inputs: 2 to 3
- Parameters: 5 (exact, read from Houdini by hython)
- Used by the height graph: no

## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/heightfield_project.html
- Summary (EN): HeightField Project projects 3D polygon geometry onto a heightfield by rasterizing each piece's distance from the heightfield's imaging plane. It blends that projected height into the input, so it can build mountains or carve valleys.
- Résumé (FR) : HeightField Project projette une géométrie polygonale sur une hauteur pour y ajouter des montagnes ou y creuser des vallées.

- Inputs meaning: ["height: input heightfield", "geometry: polygon geometry to project", "mask: optional per-pixel mask"]

- Key parameters: ["Project: rasterizes either the Minimum Height or the Maximum Height sample", "Max Projection Height: largest absolute height that can be projected; geometry outside this range is not projected", "Mask: how much of the projected height mixes with the original height", "Blend Mode: Blend, Add, Multiply, Maximum or Minimum", "Output Projection Only: outputs only the projected height values"]

- Caveats: ["The geometry input must be polygons", "It does not work on packed geometry or volumes", "It uses the Rasterize Geometry COP internally and shares that node's geometry restrictions", "For mountains, use Maximum Height with the Maximum blend; for valleys, use Minimum Height with the Minimum blend"]

